## Behavior Contract

[% if PROVIDER == "claude" %]- This skill is opt-in only. Do not make `<% cmd %>map-plan`, `<% cmd %>map-efficient`, `<% cmd %>map-check`, `<% cmd %>map-review`, or `<% cmd %>map-learn` more verbose because this skill exists.
[% else %]- This skill is opt-in only. Do not make ordinary `<% cmd %>map-*` workflows more verbose because this skill exists.
[% endif %]- Keep the checklist transient in the conversation. Do not create or update files from this skill.
- Use gender-neutral wording.
- Maintain a running Markdown checklist named `Understanding checklist` and update it as the user demonstrates understanding.
- Cover the problem/context, why it existed, alternatives or branches considered, the solution, design decisions, edge cases, and broader impact.
[% if PROVIDER == "claude" %]- Work incrementally. Do not dump the full explanation at the end.
- At natural milestones, ask the user to restate their understanding or answer a check question.
[% else %]- Work incrementally. Teach one milestone, ask for a restatement or quiz answer, then fill gaps before moving on.
[% endif %]- Multiple-choice checks are allowed, but do not reveal the answer key before the user responds.
- End only when the user demonstrates enough understanding for the selected depth or explicitly opts out.

